{"schema_version":"iteris.verification_result.v0","request_id":"verify-20260619T180514214437Z-fact-alpha-1-pec-balance-and-shifted-mag","backend":"agent","mode":"fact","claim":"Alpha=1 PEC balance and shifted magnetic identities are valid for the source Maxwell-PML system.","verdict":"accepted","passed":true,"strict_verdict":"correct","summary":"Correct. The cited proof uses the same alpha=1 Maxwell-PML equations, PEC boundary condition, positivity assumptions, and shifted-variable definitions as the source problem. The electromagnetic balance follows by multiplying by E, H_x, H_y and integrating; the principal part is the boundary flux integral int_dOmega E(H_y n_x - H_x n_y) ds, which vanishes under E=0 on the PEC boundary. The alpha=1 polarization correction is valid in the integrated L2 sense, yielding the positive added energy (1/(2 chi))||P||_2^2 and dissipation (tau/chi)||P_t||_2^2. The shifted magnetic identities follow from M_x=Q_x-mu a_x H_x, M_y=Q_y-mu a_y H_y, time-independent coefficients, and b_x+a_x=b_y, b_y+a_y=b_x; substituting Q=M+mu a H cancels the sign-indefinite magnetic square terms and leaves H_x M_x+H_y M_y.","critical_errors":[],"gaps":[],"repair_hints":"","checked_artifacts":["memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-alpha1-algebra-balance.md","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-run-20260619T173930696222Z-source-problem.md","artifacts/proofs/alpha1_algebra_balance.md","sources/energy_functional_problem.tex"],"checked_fact_ids":["fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:alpha1-algebra-balance","fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:run-20260619T173930696222Z:source-problem"],"primary_fact_ids":[],"target_artifact":null,"executor":"codex","verification_scope":"codex_agent","claim_ceiling_after_verification":"verified","agent_run_dir":"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260619T180514214437Z-fact-alpha-1-pec-balance-and-shifted-mag","agent_log":"verification/agent_runs/verify-