{"schema_version":"iteris.verification_result.v0","request_id":"verify-20260619T181255226823Z-fact-the-alpha-1-source-model-has-exact-","backend":"agent","mode":"fact","claim":"The alpha=1 source model has exact edge-PML solutions with linear H-Q growth, ruling out an unconditional positive monotone or uniformly bounded energy for all eight variables.","verdict":"accepted","passed":true,"strict_verdict":"correct","summary":"Correct. The cited proof's edge-PML construction matches the source alpha=1 Maxwell-PML equations. For constant sigma_x=s>0, sigma_y=0, the ansatz E=P=P_{z,1}=P_{z,2}=H_y=Q_y=0 with spatially constant H_x,Q_x satisfies the electric equation, the alpha=1 polarization law, the P_z equations, the H_y/Q_y equations, and PEC. The remaining source equations reduce to H_{x,t}=bH_x+Q_x/mu and Q_{x,t}=-bQ_x-mu b^2H_x with b=s/epsilon_0, so M_x=Q_x+mu bH_x is conserved and nonzero M_x gives linear growth of H_x and Q_x. The symmetric sigma_x=0, sigma_y=s>0 construction gives the same conclusion for H_y,Q_y. Since these are exact finite-energy solutions whose displayed magnetic/auxiliary variables grow linearly, any time-independent positive coercive energy controlling the displayed variables cannot be monotone decreasing or uniformly long-time bounded for all source-system data in the edge-PML regime. The predecessor alpha=1 algebra-balance fact is verified and agrees with the source equations.","critical_errors":[],"gaps":[],"repair_hints":"","checked_artifacts":["memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-edge-pml-linear-obstruction.md","artifacts/proofs/alpha1_constant_pml_cases.md","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-alpha1-algebra-balance.md","artifacts/proofs/alpha1_algebra_balance.md","verification/results/verify-20260619T180514214437Z-fact-alpha-1-pec-balance-and-shifted-mag.json","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-run-20260619T173930696222Z-source-problem.md","sources/ene