{"schema_version":"iteris.verification_result.v0","request_id":"verify-20260619T181650715321Z-fact-a-positive-augmented-zeroth-order-e","backend":"agent","mode":"fact","claim":"A positive augmented zeroth-order energy gives a Gronwall estimate for bounded nonnegative time-independent absorptions in the alpha=1 source model.","verdict":"accepted","passed":true,"strict_verdict":"correct","summary":"Correct. The source model defines the alpha=1 Maxwell-PML system with PEC boundary condition, positive material parameters, and time-independent nonnegative absorptions. The predecessor alpha=1 electromagnetic-plus-polarization balance is already verified and also checks directly against the source equations: PEC cancels the Maxwell boundary flux, and E P_t gives the positive chi^{-1} P^2/2 contribution plus tau/chi dissipation. The cited Gronwall artifact then adds the L2 derivatives of P_{z,1}, P_{z,2}, Q_x, and Q_y, each matching the source auxiliary equations. After dropping the nonpositive E^2, P_t^2, Q_x^2, and Q_y^2 terms, the remaining sign-indefinite H-square terms and mixed products are all bounded by Young's inequality using the energy weights epsilon_0 epsilon_infty, mu, chi^{-1}, and the unweighted auxiliary norms. The required coefficients are controlled by the stated material parameters and L_infty norms of sigma_x, sigma_y, sigma_x sigma_y, sigma_x(sigma_y-sigma_x), and sigma_y(sigma_x-sigma_y). Thus dE_0/dt <= C_G E_0 and Gronwall gives E_0(t) <= exp(C_G t) E_0(0).","critical_errors":[],"gaps":[],"repair_hints":"","checked_artifacts":["memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-augmented-gronwall-energy.md","artifacts/proofs/alpha1_constant_pml_cases.md","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-alpha1-algebra-balance.md","artifacts/proofs/alpha1_algebra_balance.md","verification/results/verify-20260619T180514214437Z-fact-alpha-1-pec-balance-and-shifted-mag.json","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_e