{"schema_version":"iteris.verification_result.v0","request_id":"verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m","backend":"agent","mode":"fact","claim":"The standard stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML restores planar-interface perfect matching and, in the reduced normal-incidence constant-coefficient case, has the dissipative energy identity stated in the fact file.","verdict":"accepted","passed":true,"strict_verdict":"correct","summary":"Correct within the stated scope. The cited fact is supported for the standard Laplace-domain stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML with the physical Debye law left as A(s)=epsilon0 epsilon_infty+chi/(1+tau s), coordinate-aligned planar interfaces, Re s>0, physical positive material parameters, and constant nonnegative layer damping in the reduced 1D energy calculation. The planar-interface calculation is algebraic: replacing partial_x by S_x^{-1} partial_x gives (S_x^{-1} kappa_sc)^2=kappa_0^2, so choosing the outgoing/decaying branch kappa_sc=S_x kappa_0 makes the PML admittance equal to the physical admittance and the reflection coefficient vanishes. The reduced normal-incidence system follows by multiplying the 1D stretched equations by (s+rho)/s, giving (partial_t+rho)(epsilon0 epsilon_infty E+P)=partial_x H_y, mu(partial_t+rho)H_y=partial_x E, and P+tau P_t=chi E. Multiplying by E and H_y and using E=(P+tau P_t)/chi yields exactly the stated energy derivative with the boundary flux plus the nonpositive bulk terms. The supporting artifact also correctly limits the result: it does not claim a full 2D monotone energy for the exact ADE stretched-coordinate system.","critical_errors":[],"gaps":[],"repair_hints":"No repair needed.","checked_artifacts":["verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T064808296793Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m/request.json","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-standard-stretched-pml-matching-and-1d-energy.md","artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaire