{"schema_version":"iteris.verification_result.v0","request_id":"verify-20260620T065326237995Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m","backend":"agent","mode":"fact","claim":"The standard stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye PML is perfectly matched, but the naive physical Debye energy for its full 2D ADE time-domain realization has sign-indefinite memory couplings, so the artifact only proves a reduced 1D monotone identity and identifies the full-energy gap.","verdict":"accepted","passed":true,"strict_verdict":"correct","summary":"Correct within the fact's stated scope. The stage-3 artifact proves planar-interface perfect matching for the stretched-coordinate Maxwell-Debye model by keeping the Debye law as (1+tau s)P=chi E and applying S_i^{-1} only to spatial derivatives; at an x-interface with S_y=1 the PML normal symbol satisfies nu=S_x nu0 and the admittance equals the physical admittance. The ADE realization of S_i^{-1}=s/(s+sigma_i) yields the displayed auxiliary variables, and differentiating the naive physical Debye energy gives the negative Debye dissipation term plus the memory couplings E(psi_E,x-psi_E,y)-H_x psi_Hx,y+H_y psi_Hy,x. Those auxiliary couplings have no definite sign in the physical energy alone, so the v2 monotone identity does not transfer to the exact stretched-coordinate ADE system. The same artifact and the prior accepted verification support that only the reduced normal-incidence 1D monotone identity is proved, while the full 2D monotone augmented/passive-memory energy remains an identified gap rather than a claimed theorem.","critical_errors":[],"gaps":[],"repair_hints":"","checked_artifacts":["verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T065326237995Z-fact-the-standard-stretched-coordinate-m/request.json","memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-stretched-coordinate-debye-pml-matching-and-energy-gap.md","artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md","verification/results/verify-20260620T064341474739Z-fact-the-v2-