{"schema_version":"iteris.verification_result.v0","request_id":"verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet","backend":"agent","mode":"fact","claim":"Strict decay of total electromagnetic-Debye energy on the whole computational domain is impossible without a nullspace, because nonzero stationary gradient magnetic fields can live in an undamped physical subregion with E=P=0 and zero dissipation.","verdict":"accepted","passed":true,"strict_verdict":"correct","summary":"Correct. The source model and the repaired ADE model both use the 2D TM first-order evolution equations with E, H_x, H_y, P and PML auxiliaries, and the source problem imposes PEC E=0 but no additional divergence constraint. In an open physical subregion where sigma_x=sigma_y=0, choose phi smooth, compactly supported there, with grad phi nonzero, set E=P=0, all auxiliary variables zero, H_x=partial_x phi, and H_y=partial_y phi. Then partial_x H_y - partial_y H_x=0, partial_x E=partial_y E=0, the Debye law gives P_t=0, and every PML/ADE damping or auxiliary source term vanishes. Compact support keeps boundary and interface traces harmless. Thus the state is a nonzero stationary solution with positive magnetic energy for any positive state energy controlling H. Along such a stationary state an autonomous total electromagnetic-Debye energy cannot strictly decrease for every nonzero state. Therefore a valid dissipative identity on the whole computational domain must allow a nullspace containing these undamped curl-free magnetic modes.","critical_errors":[],"gaps":[],"repair_hints":"None.","checked_artifacts":["memory/facts/fact-2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration-whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction.md","artifacts/proofs/stage3_repaired_model_energy.md","sources/energy_functional_problem.tex"],"checked_fact_ids":["fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction"],"primary_fact_ids":["fact:2d_maxwell_pml_energy_functional_exploration:whole-domain-strict-decay-nullspace-obstruction"],"target_artifact":null,"executor":"codex","verification_scope":"codex_agent","claim_ceiling_after_verification":"verified","agent_run_dir":"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet","agent_log":"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet/codex.log","agent_events_log":"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet/codex.events.jsonl","agent_stderr_log":"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet/codex.stderr.log","agent_log_manifest":"verification/agent_runs/verify-20260620T065810059861Z-fact-strict-decay-of-total-electromagnet/log_manifest.json","created_at":"2026-06-20T07:01:54.723549Z","verifier":"iteris.codex_verification_agent"}
